<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="050b" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Retire the legacy extraction path (deletion)</title>
    <phase>2 Submission and extraction (WP2)</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Pure deletion of superseded AI members, the legacy handler and their docs after 050a moved confirm onto the submission path; tagged deletion, so code-review and adr-check run regardless (root CLAUDE.md §8).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Mechanical removal guided by grep; owner decided delete (D-71) and split the redirect into 050a (D-134); ontology-r1 confirmed no dependency.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>042, 049, 050a</deps>
    <tags>bff, ai, deletion, finance</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Remove the legacy Finance extraction path now that 049 extracts through ReadInvoiceAsync and 042 classifies through ClassifyAsync: delete ExtractInvoiceFactsAsync and the extraction schema, deployment name and playbook id options, remove GetPlaybookByNameAsync and GetStructuredCompletionAsync from IInvoiceAi, and remove InvoiceExtractionJobHandler, which nothing enqueues once 050a has redirected the confirm route into 044 (owner decisions D-71, D-134) (FR-21, FR-46, D-19, D-52).</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in safe deletion with grep proof and ArchTest ratchets. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>grep finds no caller or declaration of ExtractInvoiceFactsAsync, GetPlaybookByNameAsync (on IInvoiceAi), IInvoiceAi.GetStructuredCompletionAsync, ExtractionResultSchema, ExtractionDeploymentName or InvoiceExtractionPlaybookId; IInvoiceAi keeps GenerateEmbeddingAsync and the Action-backed methods; InvoiceExtractionJobHandler and its registration are gone; ratchets shrink; publish size shrinks; tests green.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Today: InvoiceExtractionJobHandler.cs:221 calls IInvoiceAnalysisService.ExtractInvoiceFactsAsync (IInvoiceAnalysisService.cs:33, InvoiceAnalysisService.cs:118, playbook "FinanceExtraction" :41, FinanceJsonSchemas.ExtractionResultSchema :40, FinanceOptions.ExtractionDeploymentName :42) and reads FinanceOptions.InvoiceExtractionPlaybookId (:328; option :55; appsettings.template.json:454-455). Until 050a the handler was enqueued by InvoiceReviewService's confirm path behind POST /api/finance/invoice-review/confirm; 050a redirects confirm into the submission operation (D-134), so after 050a nothing enqueues InvoiceExtraction. Confirm 050a's notes (projects/ebilling-r1/notes/050a-confirm-redirect.md) for any leftover constant or member this task removes. A separate legacy tool handler, Services/Ai/Handlers/InvoiceExtractionToolHandler.cs, does not call the removed members. Ratchets naming the handler: AsymmetricRegistrationTests.cs:57-58, GateCombinationConstructibilityTests.cs:62, ADR013_LinearConsumerBoundaryTests.cs:74 (playbook-lookup baseline). Docs: finance-intelligence-architecture.md (:45, :72, :76, :174, :184) and AI-ARCHITECTURE.md:374.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/IInvoiceAi.cs, InvoiceAi.cs, NullInvoiceAi.cs (remove GetPlaybookByNameAsync, GetStructuredCompletionAsync; drop IPlaybookService / IOpenAiClient if unused except for embeddings)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/IInvoiceAnalysisService.cs and InvoiceAnalysisService.cs (remove; delete both files if empty, with their FinanceModule registration :41-45)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/Models/FinanceJsonSchemas.cs (remove ExtractionResultSchema; delete the file if empty) and the ExtractionResult model if no reader remains</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Configuration/FinanceOptions.cs (remove ExtractionDeploymentName, InvoiceExtractionPlaybookId) and appsettings.template.json:454-455 (shared append point)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/Handlers/InvoiceExtractionJobHandler.cs (removed; confirm already redirected into 044 by 050a)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/InvoiceReviewService.cs (only to remove leftovers of the legacy path that 050a left for this task, if any)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/FinanceModule.cs (shared append point; comment :23)</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/Adr032/AsymmetricRegistrationTests.cs:57-58, Adr032/GateCombinationConstructibilityTests.cs:62, ADR013_LinearConsumerBoundaryTests.cs:74 (remove entries that no longer apply)</file>
      <file role="modify">docs/architecture/finance-intelligence-architecture.md, docs/architecture/AI-ARCHITECTURE.md:374</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="042" status="required">Classification no longer uses the legacy members.</dependency>
      <dependency task="049" status="required">Extraction runs through ReadInvoiceAsync in the submission job.</dependency>
      <dependency task="050a" status="required">Confirm no longer enqueues InvoiceExtraction (D-134).</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Every change under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api follows .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-52 / FR-21">After this task no Finance or eBilling code uses by-name playbook lookup, a C# output schema or a FinanceOptions deployment name. Keep IInvoiceAi.GenerateEmbeddingAsync, InvoiceHints (classification hints) and FinanceOptions.ClassificationConfidenceThreshold.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002 / D-19">No path may create sprk_invoice except the submission job (049); 050a made confirm call the submission operation. This task changes no behaviour: it deletes only code that nothing calls after 050a.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ArchTest ratchets">Ratchet baselines only shrink: remove entries for deleted types; never add an entry.</constraint>
    <constraint source="live data">Deactivating the FinanceExtraction / PB-013 playbook rows in Dataverse needs explicit owner OK; this task records them, it does not delete them.</constraint>
    <constraint source="tests">This task deletes tests of removed members: follow docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md and docs/standards/TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md; list every deleted test and why in notes.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Deletion and AI boundary</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/ai.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-032-bff-nullobject-kill-switch.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/finance-intelligence-architecture.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context and rigor">Declare rigor STANDARD (deletion tag: code-review and adr-check run). Grep every member listed in the goal across src/, tests/, docs/ and scripts/; save the list in notes.</step>
    <step order="1">Check that 050a is merged into this branch and that nothing enqueues InvoiceExtraction (grep JobTypeInvoiceExtraction and "InvoiceExtraction").</step>
    <step order="2">Remove InvoiceExtractionJobHandler and its registration (D-71, D-134).</step>
    <step order="3">Remove the members and options listed; delete InvoiceAnalysisService / IInvoiceAnalysisService and FinanceJsonSchemas if empty; update registrations, comments and appsettings.template.json.</step>
    <step order="4">Shrink the three ArchTest baselines; update the two architecture docs.</step>
    <step order="5">Re-run grep: no remaining reference outside notes and history docs; build, full test, publish-size delta against a fresh master build (expected negative).</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]`.</step>
    <step order="7">Record deviations, the decision, deleted tests and the Dataverse rows left for owner action in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Owner decided D-71 (2026-10-15): delete the legacy extraction path. D-134 (2026-10-20) split the redirect of POST /api/finance/invoice-review/confirm into 050a. ontology-r1 confirmed on 2026-10-15 that it does not depend on the legacy handler, ExtractInvoiceFactsAsync, FinanceJsonSchemas, the by-name AI methods, sprk_billingevent, the invoice-index enqueue or PB-013 (see D-71). Preserve what FinanceBaseValues reads: submission-written invoices carry sprk_totalamount and the matter / project lookup. Send the PR to ontology-r1 for review; if the change would touch FinanceBaseValues or those columns, STOP and report.</trigger>
    <trigger>If any caller outside Finance (for example a playbook node or the tool handler) still needs a removed member, STOP and report instead of keeping the member.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ ; dotnet test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">IInvoiceAi.cs, InvoiceAi.cs, NullInvoiceAi.cs, FinanceOptions.cs, FinanceModule.cs, InvoiceExtractionJobHandler.cs (removed or redirected), deleted InvoiceAnalysisService / FinanceJsonSchemas if empty</output>
    <output type="test">Updated ArchTest baselines; updated or deleted Finance tests</output>
    <output type="docs">finance-intelligence-architecture.md, AI-ARCHITECTURE.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">grep over src/ and tests/ finds no ExtractInvoiceFactsAsync, ExtractionResultSchema, ExtractionDeploymentName, InvoiceExtractionPlaybookId, and no GetPlaybookByNameAsync or GetStructuredCompletionAsync on IInvoiceAi / InvoiceAi / NullInvoiceAi (FR-21 acceptance).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">IInvoiceAi still exposes GenerateEmbeddingAsync and every Action-backed method; NullInvoiceAi covers each remaining method.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Nothing enqueues InvoiceExtraction and no handler is registered for it (grep; 050a's test that confirm enqueues InvoiceSubmissionProcessing still passes).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no code path except 049 creates sprk_invoice (grep for creates of sprk_invoice in src/server).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The three ArchTest baselines contain no entry for a deleted type and the ArchTests pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Deleted tests are listed in notes with the removed member each covered.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish-size delta of Sprk.Bff.Api measured against a fresh master build and recorded in task notes; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build exits 0; dotnet test exits 0.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-21, FR-46, D-19, D-52. FR-46 assigns removal of GetPlaybookByNameAsync / GetStructuredCompletionAsync to the classification migration; they move here because extraction used them until 049. Shared append points: FinanceModule.cs, appsettings.template.json. Out of scope, recorded only: InvoiceExtractionToolHandler (legacy tool handler, no removed-member calls) and the Dataverse playbook rows. Split from 050 by D-134 (2026-10-20): the confirm redirect is 050a; this task is the pure deletion, its docs and the publish-size delta. #2242 (uac-r2, 2026-10-22): UpdateInvoiceExtractionStatusAsync (~:558-582) writes sprk_extractionstatus through IDocumentDataverseService.UpdateDocumentFieldsAsync(invoiceId), which targets sprk_document, so a failed extraction never marks the invoice. This task's deletion of the handler closes #2242. If UAC PR #2239 (#2237) has merged, remove its fixed-key exemption for this member from the EveryGenericUpdateWriter_AsksTheAppOnlyRefusal guard (the guard reports it stale); close #2242 in the completion commit. #2259 (uac-r2, 2026-10-22): the seeded 'Finance Invoice Processing' output mapping never wrote, because OutputOrchestratorService.ResolveComplexValue calls TryGetProperty on plain string and number JsonElements and throws. InvoiceExtractionJobHandler is that service's only caller (the other references are DI registrations in AnalysisServicesModule.cs and FinanceModule.cs). This task deletes the handler, so the mapping never starts writing, and its columns are not wanted. Remove FinanceModule's registration of the service. If nothing else references OutputOrchestratorService after that, either remove it and its AnalysisServicesModule registration or record the orphan for the AI owners; do not fix ResolveComplexValue just to make the mapping write. The completion commit closes #2259. uac-r2 2026-10-22, overlap with UAC PR #2258 (#2257, adds a person/System run identity to OutputOrchestratorService and DataverseUpdateHandler; the output-mapping write impersonates the run's person; it adds OutputMappingRunIdentityTests). Before deleting OutputOrchestratorService, check whether DataverseUpdateHandler has any other caller. If it has none, remove it or record it as an orphan. Removing it means updating the ArchTest EveryGenericUpdateWriter_AsksTheAppOnlyRefusal, which lists it as a writer; the refusal is asked at DataverseUpdateHandler.cs:59. Whichever of 050b and #2258 merges second resolves the conflict: if 050b is first, uac-r2 trims #2258; if #2258 is first, 050b deletes its hunks and OutputMappingRunIdentityTests along with the service. #2263 (uac-r2): DataverseUpdateHandler's Optimistic mode puts versionnumber in the PATCH body instead of an If-Match header, so the concurrency check is probably not enforced. Its only production caller is InvoiceExtractionJobHandler. If this task removes the handler, close #2263 with the merge SHA. If the handler survives, fix it as #2263 describes, in scope, with a must-fire test.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load every file in knowledge/files before Step 1. Follow task-execute for rigor, checkpoints and quality gates.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
